  "pull_request": {
    "number": 920,
    "title": "prove: Verify x86 AVX feature detection",
    "body": "Enable and verify `has_avx()` and `has_avx512()` in the existing x86 module, adding 16 Verified executable LoC. Per-call ghost samples specify the original leaf-0 gate and the exact AVX/AVX-512F bit checks; other inactive code and existing comments are preserved.\n\nReplace the core CPUID intrinsics with the already specified `native_cpuid::cpuid_count`. The pinned x86/raw-cpuid implementation delegates to the same intrinsic and preserves all four registers, so query arguments and order are unchanged. No trusted boundary is added. The contracts describe this invocation's samples; they do not assume consistency across reads or prove all hardware and OS conditions for executing AVX instructions.\n\nPowered by fy0/Veriflow\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Enable and verify <code class=\"notranslate\">has_avx()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">has_avx512()</code> in the existing x86 module, adding 16 Verified executable LoC. Per-call ghost samples specify the original leaf-0 gate and the exact AVX/AVX-512F bit checks; other inactive code and existing comments are preserved.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replace the core CPUID intrinsics with the already specified <code class=\"notranslate\">native_cpuid::cpuid_count</code>. The pinned x86/raw-cpuid implementation delegates to the same intrinsic and preserves all four registers, so query arguments and order are unchanged. No trusted boundary is added. The contracts describe this invocation's samples; they do not assume consistency across reads or prove all hardware and OS conditions for executing AVX instructions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Powered by fy0/Veriflow</p>",
